codex
The coverage run exposed a timing-only flaw in my baseline assertion: while a rekey is intentionally suspended, background task counts can legitimately retire between snapshots, so exact equality is not a stable “no leak” predicate. I’m changing those intermediate checks to assert no task growth plus exact socket/session/channel/allocation/buffer ownership, while retaining exact `.zero` after the rekey is released and transport closes.
